.TH RUSTY-SWEEPER 1 "October 2026" "rusty-sweeper 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rusty-sweeper \- a fast, interactive disk usage analyzer and cleaner for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rusty-sweeper
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rusty-sweeper
is a disk usage management utility that provides:
.IP \(bu 2
Interactive TUI with ncdu-like interface
.IP \(bu 2
Project detection and build artifact cleaning from within the TUI
.SH MODES
The default mode is an interactive TUI. With --cli, print a disk-usage
report and exit. PATH defaults to the current working directory.
CLI reports include hidden entries. Project cleanup is available with --cli --clean.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --cli
Print a full disk-usage tree and exit.
.TP
.B --clean
Discover projects, report artifact paths and sizes, and ask for confirmation before
cleaning. Requires --cli; conflicts with --json and --depth. Uses cleaner settings.
Deletes listed local artifacts directly without running project scripts.
Only y or yes confirms; empty input or EOF cancels.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip cleanup confirmation. Requires --clean. The report is still printed.
.TP
.B --json
Print the full scan as JSON. Requires --cli; conflicts with --depth.
.TP
.B --depth=N
Limit text display depth (root = 0). Requires --cli. Totals include all descendants.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config =\fIPATH\fR
Path to configuration file
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity (-v, -vv, -vvv)
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-essential output
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information
.SH USAGE
.B rusty-sweeper
.PP
Launch the TUI with default settings.
.SH TUI KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.BR j / \[da]
Move down
.TP
.BR k / \[ua]
Move up
.TP
.BR Enter / l / \[->]
Expand/enter directory
.TP
.BR h / \[<-] / Backspace
Collapse/go up
.TP
.BR d / Delete
Delete selected
.TP
.B c
Clean project
.TP
.B s
Cycle sort order
.TP
.B /
Search
.TP
.B .
Toggle hidden files
.TP
.B r
Rescan
.TP
.B ?
Help
.TP
.BR q / Esc
Quit
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration file: \fI~/.config/rusty-sweeper/config.toml\fR
.PP
Scanner configuration applies to both CLI and TUI scans. Cleaner configuration applies to TUI and CLI cleanup.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[scanner]
parallel_threads = 0
cross_filesystems = false
use_cache = true
cache_ttl = 3600

[cleaner]
project_types = ["cargo", "gradle", "npm", "maven"]
exclude_patterns = ["**/.git", "**/vendor"]
min_age_days = 7
max_depth = 10
parallel_jobs = 4

[tui]
color_scheme = "auto"
show_hidden = false
default_sort = "size"
large_dir_threshold = 1073741824
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rusty-sweeper/config.toml
User configuration file
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the TUI:
.B rusty-sweeper
.TP
Print a disk-usage report:
.B rusty-sweeper --cli --depth 1 /home
.TP
Export a scan as JSON:
.B rusty-sweeper --cli --json /home
.TP
Preview and confirm project cleanup:
.B rusty-sweeper --cli --clean /home/projects
.TP
Clean projects without prompting:
.B rusty-sweeper --cli --clean -y /home/projects
